# Build context exclusions for `docker compose build` / `up --build`.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
#
# Before Docker reads a single Dockerfile instruction it tars up this folder
# and uploads it to the daemon as the "build context". This Dockerfile creates
# every file it needs with heredoc COPY and reads nothing from disk, so that
# upload is pure waste -- and it is not free: a locally built
# nemohermes-api-local.tar is ~190 MB, and without the rules below it would be
# re-sent to the daemon on every single build.
#
# So this file is a build-speed optimisation, not a security control. What
# keeps secrets out of image layers is that no `COPY <path>` from the context
# exists at all. Excluding .env below is defence in depth against that changing.
#
# Add an exception here if you ever introduce a real `COPY <path>` from disk.

# Secrets and local configuration: must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.example

# Build outputs.
*.tar

# Documentation and the Compose file: read on the host, never by the daemon.
*.md
docker-compose.yml

# Editor, VCS and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.cursor
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
